/**
 * @defgroup MIDILAR_Ump Universal MIDI Packets
 * @ingroup MIDILAR_Protocol
 * @brief Containers and adapters for both MIDI protocols and other UMP families.
 *
 * UMP is a packet format, not a synonym for MIDI 2.0. Packet represents one
 * to four 32-bit words with the UMP message-type header. Group/GroupMask are
 * routing concepts belonging to UMP; channels are shared protocol concepts.
 * Packet classifies utility, system, MIDI 1.0 voice, SysEx7, MIDI 2.0 voice,
 * Data128, flex and stream messages. Classification is not typed support for
 * every family; see the individual factories.
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include <MIDILAR_Protocol.h>
 * using namespace MIDILAR::Protocol;
 * Midi::Message note1;
 * note1.NoteOn(60, 100, 0);
 * auto note2 = Midi2::Message::NoteOn(Channel::FromNumber(1),
 *     NoteNumber::FromValue(60), Midi2::Velocity::FromMidi2(50000));
 * auto group = Ump::Group::FromNumber(1);
 * auto packet1 = Ump::Encode(group, note1);
 * auto packet2 = Ump::Encode(group, note2);
 * auto bytesAgain = Ump::DecodeMidi1(packet1);
 * auto fieldsAgain = Ump::DecodeMidi2(packet2);
 * @endcode
 *
 * Midi1Parser/Midi1Encoder translate MIDI 1.0 byte streams to/from Packet.
 * DecodeUsbMidi1/UsbMidi1Encoder translate USB MIDI 1.0 events to/from Packet.
 * SysExAssembler assembles payloads from SysEx7 packets. They belong here
 * because their public interface explicitly consumes or emits UMP.
 * Native message headers do not include any of these adapters.
 *
 * Existing devices continue to exchange Packet through callbacks, so a
 * single chain can process MIDI 1.0 and MIDI 2.0 packets.
 *
 * @section MIDILARUmpMigration Namespace migration
 *
 * - Protocol::Midi1 is renamed Protocol::Midi; its headers move from
 *   Protocol/Midi1/ to Protocol/Midi/. The component represents native
 *   MIDI 1.0 bytes. Midi2 remains the native MIDI 2.0 component.
 *
 * - Protocol::Packet, Group, GroupMask, MessageType, UtilityStatus, SysExStatus,
 *   Midi1Parser, Midi1Encoder, SysExAssembler, UsbMidi1Encoder and DecodeUsbMidi1
 *   move to Protocol::Ump; their headers move under Protocol/Ump/.
 * - Protocol::Velocity, ControllerValue, PressureValue and PitchBend move to
 *   Protocol::Midi2, with their aliases in Protocol/Midi2/Values.h.
 * - Native Midi::Message no longer has ToPacket/FromPacket. Use Ump::Encode
 *   and Ump::DecodeMidi1 from Protocol/Ump/Conversion.h.
 * - Channel, ChannelMask, NoteNumber, ControllerNumber, ProgramNumber,
 *   SystemStatus, VoiceStatus, TimeCode and scaling remain in Protocol.
 * - No aliases keep the former ambiguous root names alive.
 * - Detail storage templates and tags are not public documented concepts.
 *
 * @see MIDILAR_Midi
 * @see MIDILAR_Midi2
 */
/** @namespace MIDILAR::Protocol::Ump
 * @ingroup MIDILAR_Ump
 * @brief UMP packet representation, routing groups and format adapters.
 */
